;; THE FILENAME IS HISTORICAL.  This spec once asserted that a FRAGMENT-level MMA form could
;; NOT be differentiated.  It can.  The name is kept only because 145's own record
;; (145-mma-autodiff/mma-autodiff.md:396) points at it by filename; renaming would break that
;; link to the history this spec exists to preserve.
;;
;; WHAT IT USED TO CLAIM, and why the claim was wrong — worth keeping in full, because this is
;; the clearest specimen of the mistake endeavours 145 and 146 were both about:
;;
;;     "The reason is a hardware shape contract, not a missing feature.  On a SINGLE fragment
;;      M/N/K are the native instruction shape, so the two backward GEMMs come out as
;;      dA = (M,K,N) and dB = (K,N,M) — and on either vendor exactly one of them fails:
;;        NVIDIA (16 8 8): dA fits, dB is (8,8,16) with M'=8 < M_n=16.
;;        Intel  (8 16 8): dB fits, dA is (8,8,16) with N'=8 < N_n=16.
;;      ... So the fragment forms stay a forward-only escape hatch."
;;
;; Every sentence of that is true ABOUT ONE CHOSEN LOWERING — keeping the backward in
;; registers and realising it with the same MMA instruction as the forward.  None of it is
;; true about the MATHEMATICS.  dA = dC.B^T and dB = A^T.dC hold at every shape.  145's
;; retraction routed the fragment backward THROUGH MEMORY instead, exactly as the tile-level
;; VJP already routed dC, and the lane-spanning reduction simply does not arise.
;;
;; So the negative test began failing BECAUSE THE WORK SUCCEEDED — the last artifact of a
;; retracted claim, still asserting a limitation that no longer existed.  It is now a POSITIVE
;; regression test: the same kernel, asserting it differentiates.
;;
;; VERIFIED NOT HOLLOW.  A compile that merely stops erroring proves nothing (135/01 compiled
;; with correct-looking atomics and returned 0.0).  The emitted backward here scatters
;;     ATOMIC-ADD! (~ A_GRAD m k)  <-  (~ C_GRAD m n) * (~ B k n)
;; with the mirrored loop for B_GRAD — i.e. dA = dC.B^T and dB = A^T.dC, real flow.
;;
;; THE NUMBER lives in 145/13-fragment-vjp-bmg, which gradient-checks this same
;; `store-fragment (mma-accumulate ...)` form on BMG at expect.A=1.2.  This spec covers a
;; DIFFERENT fragment shape (16x8 accumulator) and asserts compilation only; it is deliberately
;; not a second numeric check.
;;
;; COMPILE-WITH[--hardware-profile=bmg --ir-target=spv]: PASS
;; COMPILE-WITH[--hardware-profile=bmg --ir-target=spv --differentiate]: PASS
;; SKIP-DEFAULT-PASS

(def-hardware-profile bmg :simd-width 16 :mma-shapes ((8 16 8)))

(def-type a-mat (matrix float :address-space :global :align :compact :contiguous-term :row-major))
(def-type b-mat (matrix float :address-space :global :align :compact :contiguous-term :row-major))
(def-type c-mat (matrix float :address-space :global :align :compact :contiguous-term :row-major))

(def-kernel frag_mma_no_ad (A B &out C)
  (declare #'(a-mat b-mat &out c-mat)
           (global-size :set-to 16)
           (local-size  :set-to 16))
  (let ((C-acc  (make-register-fragment 16 8 0.0))
        (A-frag (load-fragment-a A (0 0)))
        (B-frag (load-fragment-b B (0 0))))
    (store-fragment (mma-accumulate C-acc A-frag B-frag) C (0 0))))
